        "id": 4405694
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-05T10:21:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it is possible. Actually this is exactly what happens when making this call:\npython3 ectool.py fpmode mode_capture pattern1 \u0026\u0026 python3 ectool.py wait_for_event fingerprint\nMKBP related interrupt is raised before response to fpmode interrupt and \u0027wait\u0027 function consumes and ignores event interrupt. I handle this by checking if there are any waiting events in cmd_wait_for_event implementation in ectool.py. I think this is sufficient for sequential processing in python tool.",
      "parentUuid": "ff2d3958_bd4889a6",
      "revId": "f3049937ce0f7f592c5ed37aa57fc6e1625c29e3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
